# Line endings are LF, on every platform, checkout included.
#
# Not a style preference — three of CI's five gates work by regenerating a file
# and diffing it (vercel.json, src/content, public/editor-*.css), and the
# generators are Node scripts that write LF. Git for Windows ships
# core.autocrlf=true, so a checkout writes CRLF and the very first
# `npm run headers` or `npm run editor` leaves a working tree that git reports
# as modified while `git diff` shows nothing at all. That state is genuinely
# hard to read, and the instinct it teaches — "commit whatever appeared" — is
# the wrong one to learn on a repo whose CI diffs generated files.
#
# eol=lf makes the checkout match what the generators produce, so the gates
# behave the same on a Windows laptop as they do on CI's ubuntu-latest.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, byte for byte.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.pdf binary
